          "case_name": "In re M.M., Juvenile",
          "citation": "2024 VT 28",
          "court": "Supreme Court of Vermont",
          "year": 2024,
          "date_decided": "2024-05-10",
          "holding": "Parents' appeal from a CHINS adjudication was dismissed as moot because the family division's jurisdiction terminated when unconditional, unsupervised custody was returned at disposition, and no mootness exception applied.",
          "relevance": "M.M. fixes when Vermont juvenile jurisdiction ends, which is the starting point for any question about continued DCF involvement with an older youth.",
          "quote": "We conclude that this case does not present a live controversy or fall within a recognized exception to the mootness doctrine and therefore grant the State's motion to dismiss.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/9501098/in-re-mm-juvenile/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 9501098
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In re R.W. and N.W.",
          "citation": "2011 VT 124, 191 Vt. 108, 39 A.3d 682",
          "court": "Supreme Court of Vermont",
          "year": 2011,
          "date_decided": "2011-11-18",
          "holding": "Termination of the mother's rights was reversed because the family division found the material change in circumstances by a preponderance rather than by clear and convincing evidence, and the ruling that the court lacked jurisdiction over the father, a Sri Lanka resident who had never been to Vermont, was also reversed, with both cases remanded.",
          "relevance": "In a footnote applying 33 V.S.A. § 5103(c) the Court states that the family division's jurisdiction will end when the seventeen-year-old child turns eighteen; that observation is dictum but is the closest Vermont appellate statement of when juvenile-court oversight of an aging-out youth stops.",
          "quote": "The court's determination of whether there has been a material change in circumstances must be by clear and convincing evidence.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1043738/in-re-rw-and-nw/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1043738
        }
